              "content": "#!/bin/bash\n# The PBS -P (--project) directive has no direct equivalent in Flux.\n# Account/project information is often handled by site-specific configurations.\n# Omission of this directive may lead to the job being charged to a default account.\n#FLUX: --queue=normal\n#FLUX: --time=00:20:00\n#FLUX: --nodes=1\n#FLUX: --exclusive\n#FLUX: --job-name=gw_amr\n\n# The previous attempt to translate 'ncpus=16' to '--ntasks=16' failed validation.\n# This suggests the system prefers node-level resource requests. The script now requests one exclusive node.\n# This provides the job with all cores on the node (satisfying the original request for 16) for the MPI application.\n\n# The PBS directive 'mem=64gb' does not have a direct equivalent as a Flux batch directive and has been omitted.\n# The performance implication is that the job may be scheduled on a node without enough memory, potentially causing it to fail.\n\n# The PBS '-l wd' directive to execute in the submission directory is the default behavior in Flux and is not needed.\n\nsource $FLUX_JOB_WORKDIR/modules.sh\n\n# The 'mpiexec' command is replaced with 'flux mini run' to launch the 16 MPI tasks within the exclusive node allocation.\nflux mini run -n 16 julia --project=$FLUX_JOB_WORKDIR -e' using GadiTutorial; main_amr(;nprocs=16,nrefs=4,num_amr_steps=6) '\n"
