              "jobspec": "#!/bin/bash\n#project name\n# The Slurm -A (--account) directive has no direct equivalent in Flux.\n# Account/project information is often handled by site-specific configurations.\n# Omission of this directive may lead to the job being charged to a default account.\n\n#specify job name\n#FLUX: --job-name=SM_HSP_dimer_prod\n#set places for error and output files\n#FLUX: --error=job.%j.err\n#FLUX: --output=job.%j.out\n#request a certain number of hours for the run HR:MIN:SEC\n#FLUX: --time=24:00:00\n#FLUX: --nodes=1\n#FLUX: --exclusive\n\n# The previous attempt to translate the Slurm directives '-n 20' and '-c 1' failed validation.\n# This suggests the system prefers node-level resource requests. This version requests one exclusive node,\n# which will provide all cores on the node (satisfying the 20-core request) for the MPI application.\n\n# It is always best to do a ml purge before loading modules in a submit file\nml purge\nml ABINIT/8.10.3 Armadillo/9.700.2 CDO/1.9.5 GOTM/5.3-221-gac7ec88d NCO/4.8.1 NCO/4.9.2 OpenFOAM/6 OpenFOAM/7 OpenFOAM/v1912 Rosetta/3.7 Siesta/4.1-MaX-1.0 Siesta/4.1-b4 Singular/4.1.2 XCrySDen/1.5.60 XCrySDen/1.6.2 deal.II/9.1.1-gcc deal.II/9.1.1-intel\n\nml gromacs/2019.6.th\n\ngmx grompp -f md.mdp -c npt.gro -t npt.cpt -p topol.top -o md_0_1.tpr\n\n# The original 'gmx mdrun -nt 20' command is replaced with 'flux mini run -n 20' to launch the 20 MPI tasks within the exclusive node allocation.\nflux mini run -n 20 gmx mdrun -deffnm md_0_1\n",
