              "content": "#!/bin/bash -l\n#flux: -N 2\n#flux: --time-limit=4h\n#flux: --exclusive\n\n# Note: Slurm -C directive (gpu) is a constraint for node features and does not have a direct Flux equivalent.\n# Performance consideration: Node feature constraints not preserved. Job may run on non-GPU nodes.\n# Note: Slurm --account directive (m1759) does not have a direct Flux equivalent.\n# Performance consideration: Account/project tracking not preserved.\n# Note: Slurm --gres directive (gpu:8) does not translate to Flux batch script directives.\n# You may need to use 'flux mini submit --gpus-per-node=8' at submission time.\n# Performance consideration: GPU allocation not specified in batch script. Job may not have access to GPUs.\n# Note: Slurm -c directive (80 cpus-per-task) does not directly translate to Flux batch directives.\n# Performance consideration: CPU allocation per task not specified.\n\nmodule load pytorch/v1.4.0-gpu\nmodule list\nexport HDF5_USE_FILE_LOCKING=FALSE\n\n# Note: Flux does not have direct equivalents to SLURM_JOB_NODELIST and scontrol.\n# Using Flux-specific commands to get node information.\nnodes=$(flux resource list -s up -no {nodelist})\nnodes_array=( $nodes )\nworker_num=$(($(flux getattr size) - 1))\n\nmaster_node=${nodes_array[0]}\n\nfor ((  i=0; i<=$worker_num; i++ ))\ndo\n  node_i=${nodes_array[$i]}\n  flux run -N 1 -n 1 --requires=\"hosts:${node_i}\" python -m torch.distributed.launch --nproc_per_node=8 --nnodes=8 --node_rank=$i --master_addr=$master_node train.py --run_num=13 &\n  pids[${i}]=$!\n  echo \"Training started on node $i\"\ndone\n\n# Wait for completion\nfor pid in ${pids[*]}; do\n    wait $pid\ndone\n\ndate\n"
