              "content": "#!/bin/bash\n# Flux submission script converted from PBS (hybrid job)\n#\n#flux: -N 4\n#flux: -n 8\n#flux: --time-limit=20m\n#flux: --job-name=test\n\n# Note: PBS -l nodes=4:ppn=8 requests 4 nodes with 8 cores per node (32 total cores).\n# This script uses 4 OpenMP threads per MPI rank with 2 MPI ranks per node (8 MPI ranks total).\n# Flux -N 4 specifies 4 nodes, -n 8 specifies 8 MPI ranks total.\n# Note: PBS -m directive (abe) does not have a direct Flux equivalent.\n# Performance consideration: Email notifications not available.\n\n# load modules\nmodule load intel/15.0.2 gcc/4.8.1 cmake/3.4.0 intelmpi/5.0.3.048\n\n# Env variables\nexport F_UFMTENDIAN=big\nexport KMP_STACKSIZE=1g\n\n# Run dir\ncd $FLUX_JOB_SUBMIT_DIR\n\n# Threads\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=4\n\n# MPI per node\nexport mpi_per_node=2\n\n# Total of MPI ranks requested\nexport mpi_sum=8\n\n# PIN THE MPI DOMAINS ACCORDING TO OMP\nexport I_MPI_PIN_DOMAIN=omp\n\n# EXECUTION COMMAND\n# Note: Using flux run instead of mpirun. -N 4 -n 8 distributes 8 ranks across 4 nodes.\n# With OMP_NUM_THREADS=4, each rank uses 4 threads, totaling 32 cores.\nflux run -N 4 -n 8 ./magic.exe input.nml\n"
